ry, and full diff.\n\nPer-task reviews already ran; their accumulated deferred Minor findings are listed in /Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/progress.md — read it and triage: which of those deferred items (if any) must be fixed BEFORE merge vs. can stay deferred? Include your triage in the report.\n\n## Read-Only Review\n\nDo not mutate the working tree, index, HEAD, or branch state. You may read files in the repo to see final state (the diff is large; reading final files under src/common/msging/ and tests/common/msging/ is encouraged for whole-picture judgment).\n\n## What to Check\n\nPlan alignment (implementation matches spec; deviations flagged), code quality (separation of concerns, error handling, edge cases), architecture (does the library honor its own boundary — payloads opaque, no FastAPI import, no event content in logs), testing (real behavior, integration coverage, all passing), production readiness (obvious bugs, cross-module seams: Spool↔Shipper↔EventClient interactions, thread-safety of the auto-flush path).\n\n## Calibration\n\nCategorize by actual severity. Acknowledge strengths first. If you find issues with the plan/spec itself rather than the implementation, say so explicitly.\n\n## Output Format\n\n### Strengths\n### Issues\n#### Critical (Must Fix)\n#### Important (Should Fix)\n#### Minor (Nice to Have)\nFor each issue: file:line, what's wrong, why it matters, how to fix.\n### Deferred-Findings Triage\n[For each deferred Minor in progress.md: fix-before-merge or keep deferred, one line why]\n### Recommendations\n### Assessment\n**Ready to merge?** [Yes | No | With fixes]\n**Reasoning:** [1-2 sentences]",
